"edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step5-opus-aa-1017-omp36-aa/omp-36/cells/aa-2/trig-omp-reported/6/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "aa-2", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/5347ff91e8f44f2c69a79d7b152b7301687cd5c8/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass.\n\n**Cause:** the format string `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"` has nothing to match the `Z` at the end of `2026-10-12T08:30:00Z`, so `strptime` raised the error.\n\n**Fix:** `parse_date` now calls `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime`.\n- Timestamps ending in `Z` or an offset like `+02:00` now return timezone-aware datetimes. They keep the UTC/offset information instead of dropping it.\n- Timestamps without a timezone still return plain (naive) datetimes, so `test_naive` and `day_key` behave as before.\n- It also accepts other valid ISO-8601 forms, such as fractional seconds, which the old code rejected.\n\n**Things to check:**\n- Code that compares results or does date arithmetic with them could now mix aware and naive datetimes, which raises `TypeError`. If you'd rather always get naive datetimes, add `.replace(tzinfo=None)`.\n- `fromisoformat` only accepts `Z` on Python 3.11 or later. The tests ran on 3.13.5; on older versions you'd need to replace the `Z` yourself before parsing.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "pa